2. Kukks' BTCPayServerPlugins — MIT
-----------------------------------
Copyright (c) Andrew Camilleri (Kukks)
https://github.com/Kukks/BTCPayServerPlugins

The BTCPay plugin patterns this repository follows descend from these plugins — specifically the
Breez, Blink and MicroNode ones: per-store Lightning client lifecycle, the Lightning
connection-string handler, the LN payment-method setup-tab UI extension points, the plugin-owned EF
schema and migrations layout, the csproj/PluginPacker packaging recipe, and the
`GetInfo -> NotSupportedException` approach for a receive-only ILightningClient.

Additionally, the *shape* of the auto-sweep settings and history UI added in Wave 4 —
Views/Spark/Sweep.cshtml and the sweep settings/record data shapes — was informed by
`TreasurySettings`, `TreasurySweepRecord` and `Treasury.cshtml` in
https://github.com/aljazceru/btcpayserver-breez-nodeless-spark, which is itself an unattributed
derivative of Kukks' MIT-licensed plugin and carries no licence file of its own. Only the
settings/UI shape was harvested. None of its sweep execution logic was used: that implementation
probes for a workable amount by trial and error, which is not an acceptable way to move money.
Attribution is recorded here to Kukks as the upstream copyright holder.


3. BoltzExchange btcpay-plugin-liquid — MIT
-------------------------------------------
Copyright (c) Boltz
https://github.com/BoltzExchange/btcpay-plugin-liquid

The sweep destination pattern is theirs: reserve a fresh, labelled address from the store's own BTC
derivation scheme via `BTCPayWallet.ReserveAddressAsync(storeId, derivation.AccountDerivation,
label)`, and rotate it per sweep. See Services/BTCPayWalletSweepAddressSource.cs. No Boltz code is
included.


